Third-party notices

Codara Studio includes code adapted from the projects below. Each entry names
what was adapted and where it lives, followed by the project's license.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Orca (https://github.com/stablyai/orca)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adapted in Codara's own idiom, not copied file for file:

- Keeping a Linux laptop awake with its lid closed: a systemd-inhibit child
  holding a block lock on sleep and the lid switch, running `cat` on a pipe
  from the app so the lock ends with the app, and the backoff after a refused
  lock (src/main/keep-awake/linux-lid-inhibitor.ts).
- Choosing the Claude Code plugin install that applies to a folder
  (installed_plugins.json, enabledPlugins in the user, project and
  project-local settings, the local, project, user order), adapted from Orca's
  src/main/skills/claude-plugin-skill-sources.ts
  (src/main/claude-plugin-skills.ts).
- The main-thread freeze watchdog: a worker thread fed heartbeats by the main
  process, with a tick-gap check that tells system sleep from a frozen main
  thread (src/main/diagnostics/hang-detection.ts,
  src/main/diagnostics/hang-watchdog-worker.ts,
  src/main/diagnostics/hang-watchdog.ts).
- The event-loop delay probe built on perf_hooks' histogram
  (src/main/diagnostics/event-loop-probe.ts).
- Crash dump pruning by size and count, and stopping Crashpad's handler when
  an AppImage exits so it does not fault after the mount goes away
  (src/main/diagnostics/crash-dumps.ts,
  src/main/diagnostics/appimage-crashpad.ts).

